// Database: mitre — the MITRE CAR data model in KQL
//
// The MITRE CAR model as KQL functions (it replaced the retired Splunk-era
// MITRE_CAR_App). Same object model,
// same coverage, same deliberate gaps — expressed as functions rather than as
// a data model with eventtypes and tags.
//
// WHY FUNCTIONS AND NOT UPDATE POLICIES
//
// An update policy writes a transformed copy into a second table on ingestion,
// and requires that "the update policy function schema and the target table
// schema must match in their column types, and order". For CAR that is the
// wrong shape: the nine objects are views over the same rows — a 4688 event is
// simultaneously an EvtxEcmdJson row and a car_process row. Materialising each
// object would double storage, force exact schema lockstep across every field,
// and make each mapping fix an ingestion-time change rather than a query-time
// one. Functions cost nothing to iterate on and match how the Splunk era
// already works: the data model is a view, not a copy.
//
// CROSS-DATABASE ACCESS
//
// Source tables live in the host / network / memory databases, so these use
// database("<name>").<Table>. That is why the databases are separate at all —
// they mirror the data domains, as intended.
//
// COVERAGE — 9 of 9 objects
//
// STRUCTURE: each object is built as one view per artefact —
// Car<Object>_<Artefact>() (e.g. CarProcess_Sysmon, CarRegistry_Memory) — which
// keeps the source table's native fields and ADDS the canonical CAR fields on top
// (car_data_model.json). The public CarX() is a `union isfuzzy` roll-up of those
// views. Filling CAR fields is the goal, not a stripping rule: native fields stay
// queryable by their own name. See docs/CAR-Extraction-Rules.md. The list below is
// the artefact -> object coverage those views implement.
//
//   CarFlow         Zeek conn + Sysmon 3 + Volatility netscan/netstat (memory)
//   CarUserSession  EvtxECmd 4624/4625/4634/4647/4648/4778/4779 (Windows)
//                   + Plaso linux:utmp:event + syslog:ssh:login (Linux)
//                   + Volatility sessions (memory — user + logon time)
//   CarProcess      EvtxECmd 4688/4689 + Sysmon 1/5, Plaso Windows execution
//                   artefacts (prefetch/amcache/appcompat), Linux cron,
//                   + Volatility pslist(+cmdline) (memory — live process tree)
//   CarService      EvtxECmd 7045/4697 + Volatility svcscan (memory — services)
//   CarFile         Plaso fs:* events + Sysmon 11/23 (create/delete)
//                   + Volatility filescan (memory-resident files)
//                   + Sysmon 12/13/14 (key/value add, set, rename)
//   CarDriver       Sysmon 6 (driver loaded) + Volatility modules (memory)
//   CarModule       Sysmon 7 (image loaded) + Volatility dlllist (memory)
//   CarThread       Sysmon 8 + Volatility thrdscan (memory — threads/start addr)
//
//   MEMORY fills ALL NINE CAR objects where dead-box cannot: Volatility 3
//   (memory.VolatilityJson) sources the live process tree (windows.piiat.processes ->
//   process, full path/parent/cmdline/DLLs), loaded modules (dlllist -> module),
//   kernel drivers (modules -> driver), connections (netscan/netstat -> flow),
//   logon sessions (sessions -> user_session), memory-resident files (filescan ->
//   file), services (svcscan -> service), threads (thrdscan -> thread, whose
//   unbacked start addresses are the injection tell) and the registry
//   the hives resident in RAM). module/driver/thread had only Sysmon before.
//
//   registry lost its only source when the KAPE path was removed; the
//   CarRegistry(). Same Zimmerman field names the old KapeJson mapping used.
//
//   driver, module, thread — SOURCED via Sysmon. Nothing *dead-box* produces
//   driver loads, image loads or thread creation, which is why they were empty
//   for so long; Sysmon (Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational, events 6/7/8) is
//   the endpoint telemetry that does, and it lands in host.EvtxEcmdJson through
//   the same EvtxECmd path as the Windows Security log. See the SYSMON note
//   below for why the PID handling differs from the Security channel.
//
// NULLS ARE PRESERVED. Where a source cannot supply a CAR field it stays null
// rather than being defaulted. A visible gap is worth more than an object that
// looks fully populated.
//
// SYSMON — a second Windows source in the SAME table.
//
// Sysmon writes to Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational, which EvtxECmd parses
// into host.EvtxEcmdJson exactly like the Security log — so Sysmon rows are told
// apart by Provider ("Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon"), not by table. The CAR
// functions below filter Sysmon branches with `Provider matches regex sysmon`
// AND the Sysmon EventId, so a stray EventId 6/7/8 from another provider (those
// numbers are reused across channels) can never leak into a Sysmon object.
//
// PID ENCODING DIFFERS. The Security channel writes ProcessId as a hex string
// ("0x1a4"); Sysmon writes it as a DECIMAL string ("420"). So Sysmon branches
// use tolong() directly and do NOT carry a pid_hex — the hex dance only the
// Security 4688 path needs. Getting this wrong would silently misparse every
// Sysmon PID, so it is called out at each Sysmon branch.

//=============================================================================
// Helper — pull a value out of an EvtxECmd Payload by Name.
//
// EvtxECmd's --json output stores EventData in Payload as JSON: an array of
// {"@Name":"X","#text":"value"} objects under EventData.Data (a field with no
// value has no "#text"). Its PayloadData1..6 summary fields vary by map, so they
// are not dependable for a specific value — hence extracting from Payload.
//
// The value is captured with an escape-aware regex, then round-tripped through
// parse_json so JSON escapes are decoded (\\ -> \ in paths, \" -> " in command
// lines). A legacy fallback matches the old XML shape (<Data Name="X">value</Data>)
// so payloads captured before the JSON switch still resolve.
//=============================================================================
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "Extract a field from an EvtxECmd Payload by Name (JSON output; falls back to the legacy XML shape)", folder = "Helpers")
EvtxPayload(payload:string, key:string) {
    let j = tostring(parse_json(strcat('"',
        extract(strcat(@'"@Name":"', key, @'","#text":"((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)"'), 1, payload),
        '"')));
    iff(isnotempty(j), j,
        extract(strcat(@'<Data Name="', key, @'">([^<]*)</Data>'), 1, payload))
}

//=============================================================================
// flow — ONE VIEW PER ARTEFACT (CarFlow_<Artefact>): source table with native
// fields kept, canonical CAR flow fields added (car_data_model.json: content,
// dest_fqdn, dest_hostname, dest_ip, dest_port, end_time, exe, flags, fqdn,
// hostname, image_path, packet_count, pid, ppid, proto_info, protocol, src_fqdn,
// src_hostname, src_ip, src_port, start_time, user). Additive; roll-up is union
// isfuzzy. See docs/CAR-Extraction-Rules.md.
//=============================================================================

// Zeek conn — the full network 5-tuple with timing and packet counts. Service is
// the app-layer protocol (proto_info); History is the connection flags. All Zeek
// columns (Uid, bytes, IpBytes, …) remain. No host/user identity (network capture).
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'flow' from Zeek conn (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/flow")
CarFlow_Zeek() {
    database("network").ZeekTyped()
    | extend
        Timestamp    = Ts,
        action       = case(ConnState == "SF", "end", ConnState == "S0", "start",
                            ConnState == "REJ", "end", ConnState in ("RSTO", "RSTR"), "end",
                            isnotempty(ConnState), "message", ""),
        src_ip       = SrcIp,
        src_port     = SrcPort,
        dest_ip      = DestIp,
        dest_port    = DestPort,
        protocol     = Proto,
        proto_info   = Service,
        ["flags"]    = History,   // `flags` is a KQL reserved word — must be bracket-quoted
        start_time   = Ts,
        end_time     = iff(isnotnull(DurationSec), datetime_add('microsecond', tolong(DurationSec * 1000000), Ts), datetime(null)),
        // Zeek omits the packet counters on some rows — a null stays null rather
        // than fabricating a 0-packet flow. Only sum when at least one is present.
        packet_count = iff(isnull(OrigPktsN) and isnull(RespPktsN), long(null),
                           coalesce(OrigPktsN, 0) + coalesce(RespPktsN, 0))
}

// Sysmon 3 (NetworkConnect) — the connection AS MADE, with the initiating process
// and user, so exe/image_path/pid/user fill; SourceHostname/DestinationHostname
// map to src_hostname/dest_hostname. No duration/packets (single event).
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'flow' from Sysmon 3 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/flow")
CarFlow_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId == 3
    | extend
        Timestamp     = TimeCreated,
        action        = "start",
        src_ip        = EvtxPayload(Payload, "SourceIp"),
        src_port      = toint(EvtxPayload(Payload, "SourcePort")),
        src_hostname  = EvtxPayload(Payload, "SourceHostname"),
        dest_ip       = EvtxPayload(Payload, "DestinationIp"),
        dest_port     = toint(EvtxPayload(Payload, "DestinationPort")),
        dest_hostname = EvtxPayload(Payload, "DestinationHostname"),
        protocol      = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Protocol"),
        exe           = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        image_path    = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        pid           = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId")),
        user          = EvtxPayload(Payload, "User"),
        start_time    = TimeCreated,
        hostname      = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn          = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
}

// Volatility netscan / netstat (memory) — connections resident in the image with
// the owning process (Owner -> image_path) and pid. action "message": observed in
// memory, not a start/end. netscan is a Win7+ pool scan (empty on XP).
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'flow' from Volatility netscan/netstat (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/flow")
CarFlow_Memory() {
    union (database("memory").VolatilityJson | where Plugin == "windows.netscan"),
          (database("memory").VolatilityJson | where Plugin == "windows.netstat")
    | extend
        Timestamp    = todatetime(Record.Created),
        action       = "message",
        src_ip       = tostring(Record.LocalAddr),
        src_port     = toint(Record.LocalPort),
        dest_ip      = tostring(Record.ForeignAddr),
        dest_port    = toint(Record.ForeignPort),
        protocol     = tostring(Record.Proto),
        image_path   = tostring(Record.Owner),
        pid          = tolong(Record.PID),
        start_time   = todatetime(Record.Created)
}


.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'flow' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarFlow() {
    union isfuzzy=true CarFlow_Zeek, CarFlow_Sysmon, CarFlow_Memory
}

//=============================================================================
// user_session — ONE VIEW PER ARTEFACT (CarUserSession_<Artefact>): native fields
// kept, canonical CAR user_session fields added (car_data_model.json: dest_ip,
// dest_port, hostname, logon_id, src_ip, src_port, user). Non-canonical logon
// detail (LogonType, SID, workstation, session type) is NOT a CAR field and stays
// in the native columns (Payload / Record). Additive; roll-up is union isfuzzy.
//=============================================================================

// Windows Security 4624/4625/4634/4647/4648/4778/4779. LogonType drives `action`
// (canonical: interactive/unlock/rdp/remote/login/logout/reconnect) but is itself
// not a CAR field, so it is computed internally and dropped; it stays queryable in
// the native Payload, as do SubjectUserSid and WorkstationName. 4624's IpAddress
// is "-" for a local logon, nulled rather than stored.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'user_session' from Windows Security logons (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/user_session")
CarUserSession_Security() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    // Channel guard: these EventIds are Security-channel events; the numbers are
    // reused by other providers, so pin the channel (non-destructive on real data —
    // EvtxECmd stamps Channel "Security" on every one of these).
    | where Channel has "Security" and EventId in (4624, 4625, 4634, 4647, 4648, 4778, 4779)
    // 4778/4779 (RDP session reconnect/disconnect) carry AccountName / LogonID /
    // ClientAddress instead of the 4624-family's TargetUserName / TargetLogonId /
    // IpAddress — coalesce per field. EvtxPayload returns "" (never null) for a
    // missing key, so the fallback is iff(isempty(...)), not coalesce().
    | extend _lt = toint(EvtxPayload(Payload, "LogonType")),
             _ip0 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "IpAddress"),
             _cip = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ClientAddress"),
             _port = EvtxPayload(Payload, "IpPort"),
             _tuser0 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "TargetUserName"),
             _auser = EvtxPayload(Payload, "AccountName"),
             _tlid = EvtxPayload(Payload, "TargetLogonId"),
             _alid = EvtxPayload(Payload, "LogonID")
    | extend _ip = iff(isempty(_ip0), _cip, _ip0),
             _tuser = iff(isempty(_tuser0), _auser, _tuser0)
    | extend
        Timestamp = TimeCreated,
        action    = case(EventId in (4634, 4647), "logout",
                         EventId == 4778, "reconnect",
                         // 4779 is a session DISCONNECT — the session ended from the
                         // user's side. CAR has no "disconnect" action, so "logout"
                         // is the nearest honest label (was: "remote", wrong).
                         EventId == 4779, "logout",
                         EventId == 4624 and _lt == 10, "rdp",
                         EventId == 4624 and _lt == 7,  "unlock",
                         EventId == 4624 and _lt == 2,  "interactive",
                         EventId == 4624 and _lt == 3,  "remote",
                         EventId == 4624, "login",
                         // 4648 = a logon USING explicit credentials — a login.
                         EventId == 4648, "login",
                         // 4625 is a FAILED logon — not a "login" in the CAR action
                         // vocabulary. action stays empty; the native EventId still
                         // identifies the failure.
                         ""),
        user      = iff(isempty(_tuser), UserName, _tuser),
        logon_id  = iff(isempty(_tlid), _alid, _tlid),
        hostname  = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        // "LOCAL" is 4778/4779's ClientAddress for a console session — not an IP.
        src_ip    = iff(_ip in ("-", "::1", "127.0.0.1", "LOCAL", ""), "", _ip),
        src_port  = iff(_port in ("-", "0", ""), int(null), toint(_port)),
        dest_ip   = "",
        dest_port = int(null)
    | project-away _lt, _ip0, _cip, _ip, _port, _tuser0, _auser, _tuser, _tlid, _alid
}

// Linux utmp/wtmp (Plaso, typed). login_type: 6/7 -> login, 8 -> logout; BOOT_TIME
// (2) is not a user session and has no canonical action, so it is excluded (still
// in the raw L2tUtmp table). Record.hostname is the login SOURCE host — not a CAR
// user_session field (no src_hostname), so it stays native.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'user_session' from Plaso Linux utmp (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/user_session")
CarUserSession_Utmp() {
    union database("host").L2tUtmp, database("host").L2tUtmpx
    | extend _lt = toint(Record.login_type), _ip = tostring(Record.ip_address)
    | where _lt in (6, 7, 8)
    | extend
        action    = iff(_lt == 8, "logout", "login"),
        user      = tostring(Record.username),
        logon_id  = "",
        hostname  = tostring(Record.image_hostname),
        src_ip    = iff(_ip in ("0.0.0.0", "", "::1", "127.0.0.1"), "", _ip),
        src_port  = int(null),
        dest_ip   = "",
        dest_port = int(null),
        SourceFile = SourceImage    // per-artefact identity for the roll-up
    | project-away _lt, _ip
}

// Linux SSH logins (Plaso ssh:login, typed): username, ip_address, port. The
// authentication_method stays native in Record.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'user_session' from Plaso Linux SSH (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/user_session")
CarUserSession_Ssh() {
    database("host").L2tText
    | where tostring(Record.data_type) == "syslog:ssh:login"
    | extend _ip = tostring(Record.ip_address)
    | extend
        action    = "login",
        user      = tostring(Record.username),
        logon_id  = "",
        hostname  = tostring(Record.image_hostname),
        src_ip    = iff(_ip in ("0.0.0.0", "", "::1", "127.0.0.1"), "", _ip),
        src_port  = toint(Record.port),
        dest_ip   = "",
        dest_port = int(null),
        SourceFile = SourceImage    // per-artefact identity for the roll-up
    | project-away _ip
}

// Volatility windows.sessions (memory) — logon sessions in the image with the user,
// Session ID (logon_id) and Create Time (logon time). Session Type stays native.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'user_session' from Volatility sessions (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/user_session")
CarUserSession_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.sessions"
    | extend
        Timestamp = todatetime(Record.["Create Time"]),
        action    = "login",
        user      = tostring(Record.["User Name"]),
        logon_id  = tostring(Record.["Session ID"]),
        hostname  = "",
        src_ip    = "",
        src_port  = int(null),
        dest_ip   = "",
        dest_port = int(null)
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'user_session' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarUserSession() {
    union isfuzzy=true CarUserSession_Security, CarUserSession_Utmp,
        CarUserSession_Ssh, CarUserSession_Memory
}

// Security 4688/4689 PIDs are hex strings ("0x1a4"); tolong() parses the 0x form
// at run time (tolong("0x1a4") = 420, verified against the emulator, issue #14).
// ppid comes from EventData's ProcessId (the creator), NOT the row's top-level
// Execution ProcessID (identical on every Security row → bogus parents).
//=============================================================================
// process — ONE VIEW PER ARTEFACT (CarProcess_<Artefact>). Each view is just the
// source table with its NORMAL FIELDS KEPT, plus the canonical CAR process fields
// added on top (car_data_model.json: command_line, exe, fqdn, hostname, image_path,
// md5_hash, parent_exe, parent_image_path, pid, ppid, sha1_hash, sha256_hash, sid,
// signer, user). See docs/CAR-Extraction-Rules.md.
//
// FILLING THE CAR OBJECT IS THE GOAL, NOT A STRIPPING RULE. The mapping is
// ADDITIVE — nothing is removed, every native field stays a queryable named column
// (Hidden, Payload, BytesSent, …), the CAR fields sit alongside them. The base
// views never combine sources; CarProcess() at the end is the downstream roll-up
// (rule 4), a union isfuzzy so it carries the CAR fields for every source plus
// whatever native columns each one brings.
//=============================================================================

// Sysmon 1 (ProcessCreate) / 5 (ProcessTerminate) — the richest single source.
// pid/ppid are DECIMAL -> tolong directly; the Hashes string splits into
// md5/sha1/sha256_hash; hostname/fqdn split from Computer. Event 1 has no SID or
// signer, so those stay empty. All EvtxECmd columns (Payload, Provider, …) remain.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'process' from Sysmon 1/5 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/process")
CarProcess_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId in (1, 5)
    | extend _Hashes = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Hashes")
    | extend
        Timestamp         = TimeCreated,
        action            = iff(EventId == 1, "create", "terminate"),
        exe               = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        image_path        = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        parent_exe        = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ParentImage"),
        parent_image_path = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ParentImage"),
        command_line      = EvtxPayload(Payload, "CommandLine"),
        pid               = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId")),
        ppid              = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ParentProcessId")),
        user              = EvtxPayload(Payload, "User"),
        sid               = "",
        md5_hash          = extract(@"(?i)\bMD5=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _Hashes),
        sha1_hash         = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA1=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _Hashes),
        sha256_hash       = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA256=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _Hashes),
        signer            = "",
        hostname          = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn              = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _Hashes
}

// Security 4688 (create) / 4689 (terminate). Carries SubjectUserSid -> sid (which
// Sysmon can't give); no file hashes. pid/ppid are HEX ("0x1a4") — tolong parses
// the 0x form. ppid is EventData's ProcessId (the creator). 4689 has only the
// terminating ProcessName/ProcessId, so parent/command_line are empty there.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'process' from Security 4688/4689 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/process")
CarProcess_Security() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    // Channel guard: 4688/4689 are Security-channel events; the numbers are reused
    // by other providers, so pin the channel (non-destructive on real data).
    | where Channel has "Security" and EventId in (4688, 4689)
    | extend
        _NewName   = EvtxPayload(Payload, "NewProcessName"),
        _Name4689  = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessName"),
        _NewPid    = EvtxPayload(Payload, "NewProcessId"),
        _EvPid     = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId"),
        _SubjName  = EvtxPayload(Payload, "SubjectUserName"),
        _SubjDom   = EvtxPayload(Payload, "SubjectDomainName")
    | extend
        Timestamp         = TimeCreated,
        action            = iff(EventId == 4688, "create", "terminate"),
        exe               = iff(EventId == 4688, _NewName, _Name4689),
        image_path        = iff(EventId == 4688, _NewName, _Name4689),
        parent_exe        = iff(EventId == 4688, EvtxPayload(Payload, "ParentProcessName"), ""),
        parent_image_path = iff(EventId == 4688, EvtxPayload(Payload, "ParentProcessName"), ""),
        command_line      = iff(EventId == 4688, EvtxPayload(Payload, "CommandLine"), ""),
        pid               = iff(EventId == 4688, tolong(_NewPid), tolong(_EvPid)),
        ppid              = iff(EventId == 4688, tolong(_EvPid), long(null)),
        // "-" is the Security channel's placeholder for an absent value — treat it
        // as empty everywhere rather than fabricating a "-\name" (or bare "-")
        // identity. XP-era 4688s carry "-" in every user field; those rows honestly
        // have no user.
        user              = iff(isempty(_SubjName) or _SubjName == "-",
                                iff(UserName in ("-", @"-\-"), "", UserName),
                                iff(isempty(_SubjDom) or _SubjDom == "-", _SubjName, strcat(_SubjDom, @"\", _SubjName))),
        sid               = EvtxPayload(Payload, "SubjectUserSid"),
        md5_hash          = "",
        sha1_hash         = "",
        sha256_hash       = "",
        signer            = "",
        hostname          = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn              = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _NewName, _Name4689, _NewPid, _EvPid, _SubjName, _SubjDom
}

// Volatility windows.piiat.processes (psscan — unlinked processes found). Full image path,
// parent path, command line, pid, ppid, create time from each process's rebuilt
// address space. No user/SID or hostname natively (honest gaps). All plugin fields
// (Record.Hidden, Record.DllCount, …) remain queryable as normal columns.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'process' from Volatility psscan (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/process")
CarProcess_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.piiat.processes"
    | extend _full = tostring(Record.Path), _short = tostring(Record.ImageFileName)
    | extend
        Timestamp         = todatetime(Record.CreateTime),
        action            = "create",
        exe               = iff(isnotempty(_full), _full, _short),
        image_path        = iff(isnotempty(_full), _full, _short),
        parent_exe        = tostring(Record.ParentPath),
        parent_image_path = tostring(Record.ParentPath),
        command_line      = tostring(Record.CommandLine),
        pid               = tolong(Record.PID),
        ppid              = tolong(Record.PPID),
        user              = "",
        sid               = "",
        md5_hash          = "",
        sha1_hash         = "",
        sha256_hash       = "",
        signer            = "",
        hostname          = "",
        fqdn              = ""
    | project-away _full, _short
}

// Plaso Windows execution artefacts (prefetch, amcache, appcompatcache, userassist,
// bam) — evidence a program ran, with image hostname and user from Plaso enrichment.
// The EXECUTED PROGRAM's path lives in a different Record field per parser — never
// in Record.filename/display_name, which name the parsed ARTEFACT file itself (the
// .pf file, the hive) and must not leak into exe/image_path:
//   prefetch       -> Record.path_hints[0] (full path); Record.executable is the
//                     bare name, kept as the exe fallback only
//   appcompatcache -> Record.path            bam -> Record.path (+ the user SID in
//                     Record.user_identifier -> sid)
//   amcache        -> Record.full_path       userassist -> Record.value_name
// amcache's Record.sha1 is the PROGRAM's SHA-1 -> sha1_hash (Record.sha1_hash would
// be the parsed hive's own hash — deliberately not used). The full Plaso Record stays.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'process' from Plaso execution artefacts (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/process")
CarProcess_Plaso() {
    union
        // L2tPrefetch carries both windows:volume:creation (volume metadata, no
        // program) and windows:prefetch:execution — only the latter is a run.
        (database("host").L2tPrefetch
         | where tostring(Record.data_type) == "windows:prefetch:execution"
         | extend _art = "prefetch"),
        (database("host").L2tWinreg
         | where Parser matches regex @"(?i)appcompatcache|userassist|programscache|amcache|bam"
         | extend _art = case(Parser matches regex @"(?i)amcache",    "amcache",
                              Parser matches regex @"(?i)userassist", "userassist",
                              Parser matches regex @"(?i)bam",        "bam",
                              Parser matches regex @"(?i)appcompatcache", "appcompatcache",
                              "winreg"))
    // prefetch has no full path on some Windows versions (path_hints empty) — the
    // executable NAME is then the only identifier, so fall back to it.
    | extend _prog = case(_art == "prefetch",   coalesce(tostring(Record.path_hints[0]), tostring(Record.executable)),
                          _art == "amcache",    coalesce(tostring(Record.full_path), tostring(Record.filename)),
                          _art == "userassist", tostring(Record.value_name),
                          tostring(Record.path))
    | extend
        action            = "create",
        exe               = _prog,
        image_path        = _prog,
        parent_exe        = "",
        parent_image_path = "",
        command_line      = "",
        pid               = long(null),
        ppid              = long(null),
        user              = tostring(Record.username),
        sid               = iff(_art == "bam", tostring(Record.user_identifier), ""),
        md5_hash          = "",
        sha1_hash         = tostring(Record.sha1),
        sha256_hash       = "",
        signer            = "",
        hostname          = tostring(Record.image_hostname),
        fqdn              = "",
        SourceFile        = SourceImage
    | project-away _prog, _art
}

// Plaso Linux cron (syslog:cron:task_run) — command line, crond worker pid, user.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'process' from Plaso Linux cron (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/process")
CarProcess_Cron() {
    database("host").L2tText
    | where tostring(Record.data_type) == "syslog:cron:task_run"
    | extend _cmd = tostring(Record.command)
    | extend
        action            = "create",
        exe               = extract(@"^(\S+)", 1, _cmd),
        image_path        = extract(@"^(\S+)", 1, _cmd),
        parent_exe        = "",
        parent_image_path = "",
        command_line      = _cmd,
        pid               = tolong(Record.pid),
        ppid              = long(null),
        user              = tostring(Record.username),
        sid               = "",
        md5_hash          = "",
        sha1_hash         = "",
        sha256_hash       = "",
        signer            = "",
        hostname          = tostring(Record.image_hostname),
        fqdn              = "",
        SourceFile        = SourceImage
    | project-away _cmd
}


//=============================================================================
// process roll-up — the downstream COMBINATION stage (rule 4). union isfuzzy of
// the per-artefact views: every row has the canonical CAR process fields, plus
// whatever native columns its source brought (null for the others). Deeper
// correlation (same real process across artefacts via host+pid+time) is a later
// analytic, done only where a shared identity key allows it.
//=============================================================================
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'process' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarProcess() {
    union isfuzzy=true
        CarProcess_Sysmon, CarProcess_Security, CarProcess_Memory,
        CarProcess_Plaso, CarProcess_Cron
}

//=============================================================================
// service — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: command_line, exe, fqdn, hostname,
// image_path, name, pid, ppid, user). Note: the service binary is image_path
// (NOT module_path — that is a module/driver-only field).
//=============================================================================

// Windows 7045 (System) / 4697 (Security) — service installed. The two events name
// their fields differently: 7045 carries ServiceName/ImagePath/AccountName, 4697
// carries ServiceName/ServiceFileName/ServiceAccount — coalesce per field.
// EvtxPayload returns "" (never null) for a missing key, so the fallbacks are
// iff(isempty(...)), not coalesce(). Channel guard: 7045 lives in System, 4697 in
// Security; the numbers are reused by other providers, so pin the channels.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'service' from Windows 7045/4697 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/service")
CarService_Evtx() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where (EventId == 7045 and Channel has "System")
         or (EventId == 4697 and Channel has "Security")
    | extend _img7045 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ImagePath"),
             _img4697 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ServiceFileName"),
             _acct7045 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "AccountName"),
             _acct4697 = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ServiceAccount")
    | extend _img = iff(isempty(_img7045), _img4697, _img7045),
             _acct = iff(isempty(_acct7045), _acct4697, _acct7045)
    | extend
        Timestamp  = TimeCreated,
        action     = "create",
        name       = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ServiceName"),
        image_path = _img,
        exe        = _img,
        user       = iff(isempty(_acct), UserName, _acct),
        hostname   = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn       = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _img7045, _img4697, _acct7045, _acct4697, _img, _acct
}

// Volatility windows.svcscan (memory) — every registered service with its binary
// and owning PID. svcscan emits THREE binary columns: `Binary` (in-memory SCM
// image path), `Binary (Registry)` (the registry ImagePath, present when the
// in-memory one is null — e.g. stopped services), and `Dll` (the hosted DLL for
// svchost services). Prefer them in that order. State/Start/Type stay native.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'service' from Volatility svcscan (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/service")
CarService_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.svcscan"
    | extend
        action     = "create",
        name       = tostring(Record.Name),
        image_path = tostring(coalesce(Record.Binary, Record.["Binary (Registry)"], Record.Dll)),
        pid        = tolong(Record.PID)
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'service' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarService() { union isfuzzy=true CarService_Evtx, CarService_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// file — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: company, creation_time, file_name,
// file_path, fqdn, hostname, image_path, md5_hash, pid, ppid, previous_creation_time,
// sha1_hash, sha256_hash, signer, user). actions: timestomp/create/delete/modify/
// read/write.
//=============================================================================

// Plaso filesystem (filestat/MFT/UsnJrnl) — MACB timeline. The three artefacts
// describe files DIFFERENTLY, so each union arm is marked and mapped per source:
//   filestat — the parsed file IS the file: filename/display_name is the path,
//              and Plaso's per-file hashes (when hashing was on) are the file's own
//              hashes -> md5/sha1/sha256_hash.
//   mft      — Record.filename is the parsed $MFT artefact itself; the file the
//              entry DESCRIBES is Record.path_hints[0] (else Record.name).
//   usnjrnl  — every event is stamped "Metadata Modification"; the real action is
//              in the USN reason bits (FILE_CREATE 0x100 / FILE_DELETE 0x200 take
//              precedence over the plain modify).
// action from Plaso's timestamp_desc otherwise; create is tested first so overlaps
// resolve to it.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'file' from Plaso filesystem (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/file")
CarFile_Plaso() {
    union (database("host").L2tFilestat | extend _art = "filestat"),
          (database("host").L2tMft      | extend _art = "mft"),
          (database("host").L2tUsnjrnl  | extend _art = "usnjrnl")
    | extend _td = tostring(Record.timestamp_desc), _fn = tostring(Record.filename), _dn = tostring(Record.display_name),
             _usn = tolong(Record.update_reason_flags)
    | extend
        action    = case(_art == "usnjrnl" and binary_and(_usn, 0x100) != 0, "create",
                         _art == "usnjrnl" and binary_and(_usn, 0x200) != 0, "delete",
                         _art == "usnjrnl", "modify",
                         _td matches regex @"(?i)creation|crtime|birth", "create",
                         _td matches regex @"(?i)modification|mtime", "modify",
                         _td matches regex @"(?i)last access|atime", "read",
                         _td matches regex @"(?i)deletion|deleted", "delete", ""),
        file_path = case(_art == "mft", coalesce(tostring(Record.path_hints[0]), tostring(Record.name), _fn),
                         iff(isnotempty(_fn), _fn, replace_regex(_dn, @"^[A-Z0-9]+:", ""))),
        // filestat only: the parsed file is the file, so its hashes are canonical.
        // For mft/usnjrnl any hash would be the $MFT/$UsnJrnl artefact's own — omitted.
        md5_hash    = iff(_art == "filestat", tostring(Record.md5_hash), ""),
        sha1_hash   = iff(_art == "filestat", tostring(Record.sha1_hash), ""),
        sha256_hash = iff(_art == "filestat", tostring(Record.sha256_hash), ""),
        hostname  = tostring(Record.image_hostname),
        user      = tostring(Record.username),
        SourceFile = SourceImage    // per-artefact identity for the roll-up
    | extend
        file_name     = replace_regex(file_path, @"^.*[\\/]", ""),
        creation_time = iff(action == "create", Timestamp, datetime(null))
    | project-away _td, _fn, _dn, _usn, _art
}

// Sysmon 11 (FileCreate) / 23 (FileDelete) — file activity with the creating
// process image and user. TargetFilename->file_path, Image->image_path, ProcessId->pid.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'file' from Sysmon 11/23 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/file")
CarFile_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId in (11, 23)
    | extend _target = EvtxPayload(Payload, "TargetFilename"), _hashes = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Hashes")
    | extend
        Timestamp     = TimeCreated,
        action        = iff(EventId == 11, "create", "delete"),
        file_name     = replace_regex(_target, @"^.*[\\/]", ""),
        file_path     = _target,
        image_path    = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        pid           = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId")),
        user          = EvtxPayload(Payload, "User"),
        // Sysmon 23 (FileDelete) carries the deleted file's Hashes — extract them
        // into the canonical file hash fields, as CarProcess/Module/Driver do.
        md5_hash      = extract(@"(?i)\bMD5=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha1_hash     = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA1=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha256_hash   = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA256=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        hostname      = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn          = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, ""),
        creation_time = iff(EventId == 11, TimeCreated, datetime(null))
    | project-away _target, _hashes
}

// Volatility windows.filescan (memory) — FILE_OBJECTs resident at capture (incl.
// files deleted from disk but still in RAM). No MACB/process context and no
// canonical action fits "was resident", so action is empty — the row is a file
// OBSERVATION (path/name). Name stays native.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'file' from Volatility filescan (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/file")
CarFile_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.filescan"
    | extend _fp = tostring(Record.Name)
    | where isnotempty(_fp)
    | extend
        action    = "",
        file_path = _fp,
        file_name = replace_regex(_fp, @"^.*[\\/]", "")
    | project-away _fp
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'file' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarFile() { union isfuzzy=true CarFile_Plaso, CarFile_Sysmon, CarFile_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// registry — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: data, fqdn, hive, hostname,
// image_path, key, pid, type, user, value). actions: add/edit/remove.
//=============================================================================


// Sysmon 12 (key add/delete), 13 (value set), 14 (rename) — the CHANGE as it
// happens, so action is canonical from EventType (add/remove/edit).
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'registry' from Sysmon 12/13/14 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/registry")
CarRegistry_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId in (12, 13, 14)
    | extend _etype = EvtxPayload(Payload, "EventType"), _target = EvtxPayload(Payload, "TargetObject")
    | extend
        Timestamp  = TimeCreated,
        action     = case(_etype contains "Delete", "remove", _etype contains "Create", "add",
                         _etype contains "Set", "edit", _etype contains "Rename", "edit", "edit"),
        key        = _target,
        value      = iff(EventId == 13, replace_regex(_target, @"^.*\\", ""), ""),
        data       = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Details"),
        type       = "",
        hive       = "",
        image_path = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        pid        = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId")),
        user       = EvtxPayload(Payload, "User"),
        hostname   = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn       = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _etype, _target
}

// the hives resident in RAM. Snapshot -> action "edit". user recovered from the
// per-user hive path.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'registry' from Volatility windows.piiat.registry (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/registry")
CarRegistry_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.piiat.registry"
    | extend
        Timestamp  = todatetime(Record.LastWrite),
        action     = "edit",
        key        = tostring(Record.Key),
        value      = tostring(Record.ValueName),
        data       = tostring(Record.ValueData),
        type       = tostring(Record.ValueType),
        hive       = tostring(Record.Hive),
        user       = extract(@"(?i)(?:Documents and Settings|Users)\\([^\\]+)\\", 1, tostring(Record.Hive))
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'registry' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarRegistry() { union isfuzzy=true CarRegistry_Sysmon, CarRegistry_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// module — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: base_address, fqdn, hostname,
// image_path, md5_hash, module_name, module_path, pid, sha1_hash, sha256_hash,
// signer, tid). actions: load/unload.
//=============================================================================

// Sysmon 7 (Image loaded) — ImageLoaded is the module (module_path), Image is the
// loading process (image_path). Hashes split into md5/sha1/sha256_hash; Signature
// -> signer. Signed/SignatureStatus stay native in Payload.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'module' from Sysmon 7 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/module")
CarModule_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId == 7
    | extend _loaded = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ImageLoaded"), _hashes = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Hashes")
    | extend
        Timestamp   = TimeCreated,
        action      = "load",
        module_path = _loaded,
        module_name = replace_regex(_loaded, @"^.*[\\/]", ""),
        image_path  = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Image"),
        pid         = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "ProcessId")),
        md5_hash    = extract(@"(?i)\bMD5=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha1_hash   = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA1=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha256_hash = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA256=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        signer      = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Signature"),
        hostname    = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn        = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _loaded, _hashes
}

// Volatility windows.dlllist (memory) — every module mapped into each live process
// with its base address and load time. Path->module_path, Process->image_path.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'module' from Volatility dlllist (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/module")
CarModule_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.dlllist"
    | extend
        Timestamp    = todatetime(Record.LoadTime),
        action       = "load",
        module_name  = tostring(Record.Name),
        module_path  = tostring(Record.Path),
        image_path   = tostring(Record.Process),
        pid          = tolong(Record.PID),
        // REPRESENTATION NOTE: Volatility 3 serialises Hex renderers as plain ints,
        // so base_address is DECIMAL ("1213726720") while Sysmon's is 0x-hex
        // ("0x00060000"). NOT normalised to hex here: x64 kernel addresses
        // (0xFFFFF800...) exceed int64, so tohex(tolong(...)) would null exactly
        // the rows that matter. Compare across sources via tolong()/parse.
        base_address = tostring(Record.Base)
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'module' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarModule() { union isfuzzy=true CarModule_Sysmon, CarModule_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// driver — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: base_address, fqdn, hostname,
// image_path, md5_hash, module_name, sha1_hash, sha256_hash, signer). A driver
// loads into the kernel, so ImageLoaded IS image_path (driver has no module_path).
//=============================================================================

// Sysmon 6 (Driver loaded) — the signature fields are the point (unsigned driver =
// BYOVD tell). ImageLoaded->image_path, Hashes split, Signature->signer.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'driver' from Sysmon 6 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/driver")
CarDriver_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId == 6
    | extend _loaded = EvtxPayload(Payload, "ImageLoaded"), _hashes = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Hashes")
    | extend
        Timestamp   = TimeCreated,
        action      = "load",
        module_name = replace_regex(_loaded, @"^.*[\\/]", ""),
        image_path  = _loaded,
        md5_hash    = extract(@"(?i)\bMD5=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha1_hash   = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA1=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        sha256_hash = extract(@"(?i)\bSHA256=([0-9A-Fa-f]+)", 1, _hashes),
        signer      = EvtxPayload(Payload, "Signature"),
        hostname    = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer),
        fqdn        = iff(Computer contains ".", Computer, "")
    | project-away _loaded, _hashes
}

// Volatility windows.modules (memory) — loaded kernel modules/drivers with base
// address. Path->image_path (the driver binary), no load time in the module list.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'driver' from Volatility modules (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/driver")
CarDriver_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.modules"
    | extend
        action       = "load",
        module_name  = tostring(Record.Name),
        image_path   = tostring(Record.Path),
        base_address = tostring(Record.Base)   // decimal, not 0x-hex — see CarModule_Memory note
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'driver' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarDriver() { union isfuzzy=true CarDriver_Sysmon, CarDriver_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// thread — per-artefact (car_data_model.json: hostname, src_pid, src_tid,
// stack_base, stack_limit, start_address, start_function, start_module,
// start_module_name, subprocess_tag, tgt_pid, tgt_tid, user, user_stack_base,
// user_stack_limit). actions: create/suspend/terminate/remote_create.
//=============================================================================

// Sysmon 8 (CreateRemoteThread) — cross-process injection: Source creates a thread
// in Target. action "remote_create". Source/TargetImage are not CAR thread fields
// (thread has no image), so they stay native in Payload; the CAR mapping is the
// src/tgt pids, the new tid and the start address/module.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'thread' from Sysmon 8 (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/thread")
CarThread_Sysmon() {
    database("host").EvtxEcmdJson
    | where Provider matches regex @"(?i)sysmon" and EventId == 8
    | extend _sm = EvtxPayload(Payload, "StartModule")
    | extend
        Timestamp         = TimeCreated,
        action            = "remote_create",
        src_pid           = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "SourceProcessId")),
        tgt_pid           = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "TargetProcessId")),
        tgt_tid           = tolong(EvtxPayload(Payload, "NewThreadId")),
        start_address     = EvtxPayload(Payload, "StartAddress"),
        start_module      = _sm,
        start_module_name = replace_regex(_sm, @"^.*[\\/]", ""),
        start_function    = EvtxPayload(Payload, "StartFunction"),
        hostname          = iff(Computer contains ".", tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]), Computer)
    | project-away _sm
}

// Volatility windows.thrdscan (memory) — every thread with its owning process (PID
// -> tgt_pid), TID, create time and Win32 start address/path. Owner view, so src_*
// is empty; a start address with no backing Win32StartPath is the injection tell.
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "CAR 'thread' from Volatility thrdscan (memory) (native fields + CAR fields)", folder = "CAR/thread")
CarThread_Memory() {
    database("memory").VolatilityJson
    | where Plugin == "windows.thrdscan"
    | extend _sm = tostring(coalesce(Record.Win32StartPath, Record.StartPath))
    | extend
        Timestamp         = todatetime(Record.CreateTime),
        // thrdscan surfaces exited threads too (ExitTime set) — those are a
        // terminate, not a create.
        action            = iff(isnotempty(tostring(Record.ExitTime)), "terminate", "create"),
        tgt_pid           = tolong(Record.PID),
        tgt_tid           = tolong(Record.TID),
        start_address     = tostring(Record.Win32StartAddress),   // decimal, not 0x-hex — see CarModule_Memory note
        start_module      = _sm,
        start_module_name = replace_regex(_sm, @"^.*[\\/]", "")
    | project-away _sm
}

.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "MITRE CAR 'thread' object — roll-up of the per-artefact views", folder = "CAR")
CarThread() { union isfuzzy=true CarThread_Sysmon, CarThread_Memory }

//=============================================================================
// CarCoverage — which objects actually have data.
//
// The equivalent of `| tstats count FROM datamodel=MITRE_CAR BY nodename` on
// the Splunk era. Run this first after ingesting: an object that should be
// populated and is not means the mapping is wrong, not that the model is.
//
// All nine objects now have a source and count real rows: driver, module and
// thread from Sysmon (events 6/7/8), the other six as before. An object that
// should be populated and shows 0 means the mapping is wrong (or that source
// was not ingested), not that the model is — e.g. driver/module/thread show 0
// on a host with no Sysmon, which is expected, not a defect.
//=============================================================================
.create-or-alter function
with (docstring = "Row counts per CAR object (all nine are sourced)", folder = "CAR")
CarCoverage() {
    union
        (CarFlow()        | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "flow"),
        (CarUserSession() | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "user_session"),
        (CarProcess()     | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "process"),
        (CarService()     | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "service"),
        (CarFile()        | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "file"),
        (CarRegistry()    | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "registry"),
        (CarDriver()      | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "driver"),
        (CarModule()      | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "module"),
        (CarThread()      | summarize Rows = count() | extend Object = "thread")
    | project Object, Rows
    | order by Rows desc
}

//#############################################################################
//# MATERIALIZED CAR (epic #86) — the CAR objects as INGESTED TABLES
//#############################################################################
//
// The functions above build CAR at query time from the raw host/network/memory
// tables. In parallel, the pipeline now NORMALISES each source into finished CAR
// events (PIIAT-MitreCar: one car.db per source) and exports one
// `car_<object>.jsonl` per populated object. The tables below ingest that JSON
// 1:1 — the JSON is the ADX contract. Extraction happens ONCE, in the engine
// (its own test suite), instead of being re-derived in KQL per artefact.
//
// ADDITIVE, ON PURPOSE. These live alongside the query-time Car*() functions,
// they do not replace them yet: the ingest lane does not load car_*.jsonl until
// its SOURCES entry is added, and `verify-car` still asserts against the
// functions. Once the materialised path is wired and the verify harness is
// migrated, the query-time views collapse into these tables.
//
// SHAPE (every table): car_object (constant per table) + the common CAR header
// (timestamp, car_action, guid, owning_guid, link_confidence, source_artefact,
// source_host) + native (dynamic — evidence with no CAR home) + the object's
// MITRE fields as nullable strings. Numeric-looking fields stay string (the
// evidence is inconsistent about type); cast at query time, as VolatilityJson does.
//
// GENERATED from the engine's object model (store.HEADER + each object's fields);
// re-derive rather than hand-editing if the model changes.

//=============================================================================
// car_authentication
//=============================================================================
.create-merge table car_authentication (
    car_object:string,
    timestamp:datetime,
    car_action:string,
    guid:string,
    owning_guid:string,
    link_confidence:string,
    source_artefact:string,
    source_host:string,
    native:dynamic,
    app_name:string,
    method:string,
    auth_service:string,
    auth_target:string,
    target_ad_domain:string,
    decision_reason:string,
    response_time:string,
    fqdn:string,
    hostname:string,
    ad_domain:string,
    uid:string,
    user_role:string,
    user_type:string,
    user:string,
    user_agent:string,
    target_uid:string,
    target_user_role:string,
    target_user_type:string,
    target_user:string
)

